course: dictionary
lesson: 5583
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. Levy is a noun or a verb. A levy is a tax or charge that people must pay, and to levy is to make people pay it. Read the words around the word to find out which meaning is right.
explain: «In 1994 pieces of the comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 crashed into Jupiter, leaving dark scars bigger than the Earth.» Here Levy is not a tax at all. It is part of a comet's name. The clues are comet, crashed and Jupiter, and none of them is about money.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The council will levy a charge on plastic bags» works, because a charge is something people pay. Swap in a name and the sentence still has a comet in it, so you know the word is a name, not a tax.
fact: A levy is a tax or charge that people or companies must pay.
fact: To levy a tax or fine means to make people pay it.
fact: In history, a levy was a group of soldiers called up to fight.
fact: Everyday examples include a sugar levy on fizzy drinks and a plastic bag levy.
fact: «Shoemaker-Levy 9» is the name of a comet, named after people, so Levy in that name is not the tax word.
exercise: «The council wants to levy a charge on plastic bags.» What does levy mean here? | To write a long letter | To smash into something hard | To feel very tired | *To make people pay a charge
exercise: In the sentence «In 1994 pieces of the comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 crashed into Jupiter», what is Levy? | *A name, part of a comet's name | A group of soldiers | A kind of fizzy drink | A tax people must pay
exercise: In history, what was a levy? | A map of the stars | *A group of soldiers called up to fight | A sweet cake eaten at feasts | A tall tower on a castle wall
test: «The school will levy a fine on late library books.» What does levy mean? | To read very fast | To lend books to friends | To lose a book | *To make people pay a fine
test: Which phrase means to charge people a tax? | Plant a tree | *Levy a tax | Build a bridge | Sing a song
exam: Which sentence uses levy as a name, not as a tax? | «The king had to levy troops for the war.» | «The shop will levy a charge on plastic bags.» | *«In 1994 pieces of the comet Shoemaker-Levy 9 crashed into Jupiter, leaving dark scars bigger than the Earth.» | «Every family pays a levy on fizzy drinks.»
